From 2a9774817c1edc05f6842153c28a63d8928e283c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:29:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fontique: a query keeps what the last one matched

Parley makes a query each time it shapes a text layout, and another for
its line metrics, and each query began by clearing the collection's
query state. Every layout then listed its font stack's families again,
looked each one up, matched it and loaded its fonts, and dropped all of
it at the end. The families a query matched and the fonts it loaded
from them now outlive it: a query that sets the same families keeps
their matches, the same fallback key keeps its fallback families, and
fonts are matched again only for other attributes. A query that sets
no families, or no fallbacks, still matches none. Whatever changes the
collection (registering or unregistering fonts, a generic family or a
fallback list set, clearing, loading fonts), or a shared collection's
new version, forgets all of it.
